---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/baseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/pageHeader.astro";
import PageFooter from "../components/pageFooter.astro";
import PlaneWing from "../assets/images/teamPhotos/PlaneWing.png";
import ComputerPpl from "../assets/images/teamPhotos/Brainstorm.png";
import AeroImg from "../assets/images/teamPhotos/A&P.png";
import PlaneLgo from "../assets/images/teamPhotos/planes&logo.png";
import "../styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <PageHeader />
  <main class="Container">
    <section class="whoWeAre">
      <div class="description">
        <p class="descriptionText">
          We are a student design team at Memorial University of Newfoundland, designing a 
          fixed-wing drone to compete in the iMeche UAV Challenge. 
          Our team is made up of students from a variety of disciplines, including mechanical engineering,
          mechatronics engineering, process engineering, electrical engineering, computer engineering, 
          computer science, and business. We consist of four sub-teams: Structures, 
          Flight Systems, Aerodynamics & Propulsion, and Outreach & Administration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="structuralWing">
      <div class="description">
        <img src={PlaneWing.src} alt="" />
        <p class="descriptionText">
          The Structures sub-team is responsible for the physical design,
          analysis, and fabrication of the aircraft. This team handles the
          physical reality of the vehicle-ensuring it is lightweight enough to
          fly, strong enough to survive flight forces, and capable of being built
          within a student workshop.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flightSystems">
      <div class="description">
        <img src={ComputerPpl.src} alt="" />
        <p class="descriptionText">
          The Flight Systems sub-team is responsible for the intelligence,
          control, and operational command of the aircraft. This team handles the
          digital and behavioral reality of the vehicle-ensuring the aircraft can
          safely communicate with the ground, execute precise flight paths, and
          seamlessly transition between manual piloting and fully autonomous
          flight.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="nightHawk">
      <div class="description">
        <img src={AeroImg.src} alt="" />
        <p class="descriptionText">
          The Aerodynamics & Propulsion sub-team is responsible for the flight
          performance, stability, and power systems of the aircraft. This team
          handles the theoretical and electrical reality of the vehicle-ensuring
          the aircraft generates enough lift to fly, remains stable in the air,
          and has a reliable power system to sustain flight.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="spirit">
      <div class="description">
        <img src={PlaneLgo.src} alt="" />
        <p class="descriptionText">
          The Outreach & Administration sub-team is responsible for the
          organizational backbone, financial health, and public presence of the
          team. This team handles the logistical and operational reality of the
          project-managing team structure, securing funding, ensuring competition
          compliance, and building a professional brand identity that connects the
          team with sponsors and the community.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <PageFooter />
</BaseLayout>
